OpenCode Go Widget for Debian/Ubuntu
===================================

The package installs two halves:

  /usr/lib/opencode-go-widget
      GTK app: API key, polling and desktop card
  /usr/share/gnome-shell/extensions/ocg-usage@local
      Panel ring, weekly label and dropdown

Enable the extension for your user
----------------------------------
System extensions are installed but not enabled automatically:

  gnome-extensions enable ocg-usage@local

If that reports that the extension does not exist, log out and back in once,
then run it again. The extension loads immediately after enabling.

Start the app
-------------
Launch "OpenCode Go Widget" from the app grid, open Settings, paste your
OpenCode Go API key and press Test connection, then Save. The key is stored
per user in ~/.config/opencode-go-widget/token (mode 0600).

Autostart is off by default. Enable "Start automatically at login" in
Settings.

Removing the package
--------------------
  sudo apt remove opencode-go-widget

Your settings and API key in ~/.config/opencode-go-widget and the cache in
~/.cache/opencode-go-widget are deliberately left behind. If you enabled
autostart, turn it off in Settings before removing, or delete
~/.config/autostart/opencode-go-widget.desktop. Log out and back in to drop
the panel item.
